ID: B3-Ch06a-Hadrik-Plan
TEXT:


set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_aura_hardening >= 2 || v_combat_technique >= 1)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_aura_hardening < 2 && v_combat_technique < 1)
#if(v_b3_ch6_plan == 0 && v_combat_technique >= 1) {
"Melindra's wind control is too volatile," I say. "Holding the barrier yesterday doesn't guarantee stability today. Let Hadrik draw the initial volley."

"Keep moving," Hadrik says. "I'll turn these flying kettles into scrap."

His form shrinks, feathers sprouting along his arms as he shifts into a massive golden eagle. He launches upward, shrieking into the lead formation. Ten feet above the rooftops he snaps back to dwarven shape, drives a heavy leather boot into the optic lens of the nearest sphere, and sends it spinning into the masonry below.

"Why encourage him?" Kate mutters as we sprint through the alley mouth. "He can't hold fifty of them alone."

"He doesn't have to," I say. "He absorbs punishment better than the rest of us combined. He shatters the front rank, and we handle the spillover."

"The spillover is thirty drones," Kate says.

As Kate warns, the swarm computes Hadrik's lone disruption, delegates three units to pin him, and routes the main swarm straight at our sprinting line.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_plan == 0 && v_combat_technique < 1) {
"Melindra's wind control is too volatile," I say. "Holding the barrier yesterday doesn't guarantee stability today. Let Hadrik draw the initial volley."

"Keep moving," Hadrik says. "I'll turn these flying kettles into scrap."

His form shrinks, feathers sprouting along his arms as he shifts into a massive golden eagle. He launches upward, shrieking into the lead formation. Ten feet above the rooftops he snaps back to dwarven shape, drives a heavy leather boot into the optic lens of the nearest sphere, and sends it spinning into the masonry below.

"Why encourage him?" Kate mutters as we sprint through the alley mouth. "He can't hold fifty of them alone."

"He doesn't have to," I say. "He absorbs punishment better than the rest of us combined. He shatters the front rank, and we handle the spillover."

"The spillover is thirty drones," Kate says.

As Kate warns, the swarm computes Hadrik's lone disruption, delegates three units to pin him, and routes the main swarm straight at our sprinting line.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_plan == 2 && v_combat_technique >= 1) {
As Kate warns, the swarm computes Hadrik's lone disruption, delegates three units to pin him, and routes the main swarm straight at our sprinting line.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_plan == 2 && v_combat_technique < 1) {
As Kate warns, the swarm computes Hadrik's lone disruption, delegates three units to pin him, and routes the main swarm straight at our sprinting line.

}
A wall of bronze spheres drops into the lane fifty paces ahead, red lenses glowing as energy crackles across their weapon ports.

"Clear a corridor," Daren shouts, drawing sword and shield. "Form up!"

"No," I say. "You and Kelrim push through. Take Hadrik to punch through the line. We pull the swarm into the air and keep their guns off you."

"Kelrim is our only navigator!" Daren yells over the rising whine of turbines. "You'll lose us in the district!"

"We track you from above," I say. "Melindra can lock your aura. Move! Hadrik, carve a hole for Daren!"

Hadrik drops from a roof ledge in dwarf form, smashing two spheres together with a ringing clang. Daren, Kelrim, and Hadrik bull-rush through the gap toward the apothecary.

Melindra flicks her fingers. Rushing air curls around my boots, lifting me ten feet off the flagstones. Flower ignites twin jets of orange flame beneath her bare heels, soaring alongside Kate, who rides a rising stair of frost. Leila stays low, daggers flashing as she intercepts low-altitude sweepers.

I unlimber my crossbow, cocking the stirrup with one smooth pull and snapping a steel bolt into the groove.

#if(v_combat_technique >= 1) {
My combat technique training keeps the chaotic crossfire readable. I track the micro-rotations of the bronze casings, anticipating discharge angles before the beams fire. In the air beside me, Flower unleashes crackling firebolts while Kate skewers optics with high-velocity ice shards. Below, Leila's silver daggers sever propulsion housings before the drones can stabilize.

We grind down their frontline until the surviving spheres break formation and retreat in a high climbing bank.

Down the avenue, Daren, Kelrim, and Hadrik emerge from Pete's storefront, satchels slung across their shoulders. We drop out of the sky to meet them on the cobblestones.

}
#if(v_aura_hardening >= 2 && v_combat_technique < 1) {
The swarm overwhelms my field of view. A bronze sphere drops from a blind angle behind my shoulder, its condenser whining as it discharges a direct lightning bolt into my back.

The shock slams into my spine, but my hardened aura and lessathi electrical resistance absorb the fatal surge. Pain burns along my ribs, but my fingers hold the trigger. I spin mid-air and drill a crossbow bolt straight through the drone's glowing red eye. The sphere detonates in a shower of copper shavings.

The remaining drones register the casualty rate, break formation, and retreat in a high climbing bank.

Down the avenue, Daren, Kelrim, and Hadrik emerge from Pete's storefront, satchels slung across their shoulders. We drop out of the sky to meet them on the cobblestones.

}
#if(v_aura_hardening < 2 && v_combat_technique < 1) {
The swarm overwhelms my field of view. A bronze sphere drops from a blind angle behind my shoulder, its condenser whining as it discharges a direct lightning bolt into my back.

The electric surge bypasses my thin defenses, roasting my nervous system in an instant. My lungs seize. The crossbow slips from numb fingers. The cobblestones rush up to meet me, and darkness swallows the street.

}
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06a-Entrance, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06a-Entrance) if (v_aura_hardening >= 2 || v_combat_technique >= 1)
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_aura_hardening < 2 && v_combat_technique < 1)
