choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_aura_hardening < 2 && v_combat_technique < 1)


ID: B3-Ch06a-Rose-Awake
TEXT:

"Rose can buy us a lane," I say. "If she halts time for thirty seconds like yesterday, we can reach the threshold without firing a shot."

"She nearly collapsed holding that spell yesterday," Kate says sharply. "I won't risk her health when we have steel and magic on the field."

"Even fifteen seconds breaks their net," I say. "I'll tell her to drop the anchor the moment she feels strain. Hold on."

I unclip the transceiver, spin the dial to Rose's rune, and tap the plate.

"Rose? Are you by the line?"

"I'm here," Rose's voice answers over the soft sizzle of a skillet. "What is it?"

"We have a swarm of mechanical sentinels boxing our street," I say.

"Sentinels?" Rose sounds puzzled. "What sentinels?"

"No time to explain," I say. "Can you lock time across the district, excluding our party? You don't need a full half-minute—fifteen seconds gives us an open door."

Silence stretches over the line.

"Rose? Are you weaving the field, or—"

The roar of drone thrusters cuts off instantly. The bronze spheres freeze motionless in mid-air, suspended against the gray sky like pinned insects. The whole city falls dead still.

"We have it!" I tell the device. "Keep the thread steady for ten more—"

The hum of turbines snarls back to life. Above us, the spheres bank and dive, the spell snapping apart after barely three seconds.

"I'm sorry!" Rose's voice trembles through the speaker. "I'm so sorry... my head is pounding, and the threads kept slipping through my fingers."

"Don't apologize," I say. "We woke you after an hour of rest. The fault is mine. Get back to the stove and rest. We'll handle the rest."

"Be careful!"

I slap the transceiver shut and pocket it on the run. "The net is still live. Plan B."

"On it!" Hadrik shouts. "Keep moving!"

His form shrinks, feathers sprouting along his arms as he shifts into a massive golden eagle. He launches upward, shrieking into the lead formation. Ten feet above the rooftops he snaps back to dwarven shape, drives a heavy leather boot into the optic lens of the nearest sphere, and sends it spinning into the masonry below.

"Why encourage him?" Kate mutters as we sprint through the alley mouth. "He can't hold fifty of them alone."

"He doesn't have to," I say. "He absorbs punishment better than the rest of us combined. He shatters the front rank, and we handle the spillover."

"The spillover is thirty drones," Kate says.

choice("Continue", B3-Ch06a-Hadrik-Plan, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06a-Hadrik-Plan)


ID: B3-Ch06a-Kate-Plan
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_aura_hardening >= 3 || v_combat_technique >= 2)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_aura_hardening < 3 && v_combat_technique < 2)
#if(v_combat_technique >= 2) {
"Kate's right, Hadrik," I say. "Her ice bursts clear wide arcs in the air. We need area control, not single punches."

"Fine," Hadrik grunts, angling toward the front. "I'll clear the ground-level scrap."

"Melindra, with me," Kate says, stamping her boot to summon a flat disc of solid blue ice.

Melindra frowns at the rising disc. "My air currents are erratic today. I cannot guarantee a stable barrier under heavy bombardment."

"Step onto the frost," Kate says. "We adapt as we climb."

Melindra steps onto the platform. The ice disc lifts vertically on frost plumes, carrying them twenty feet into the crossfire.

"Keep your legs moving!" Daren shouts, shielding Kelrim with his armored shoulder.

I glance upward as we sprint. The bronze spheres converge on the rising platform, discharging crackling elemental lances. Melindra's wind barrier bends and flickers, buffeted by lightning and kinetic slugs. The gale shudders on the verge of total collapse.

}
#if(v_combat_technique < 2) {
"Kate's right, Hadrik," I say. "Her ice bursts clear wide arcs in the air. We need area control, not single punches."

"Fine," Hadrik grunts, angling toward the front. "I'll clear the ground-level scrap."

"Melindra, with me," Kate says, stamping her boot to summon a flat disc of solid blue ice.

Melindra frowns at the rising disc. "My air currents are erratic today. I cannot guarantee a stable barrier under heavy bombardment."

"Step onto the frost," Kate says. "We adapt as we climb."

Melindra steps onto the platform. The ice disc lifts vertically on frost plumes, carrying them twenty feet into the crossfire.

"Keep your legs moving!" Daren shouts, shielding Kelrim with his armored shoulder.

I glance upward as we sprint. The bronze spheres converge on the rising platform, discharging crackling elemental lances. Melindra's wind barrier bends and flickers, buffeted by lightning and kinetic slugs. The gale shudders on the verge of total collapse.

}
#if(v_aura_hardening >= 3 && v_combat_technique < 2) {
"Daren, push for the shop," I call out. "Flower and I are backing them up. That barrier is about to crack."

"Petal and I are airborne!" Flower shouts, twin jets of orange fire flaring from her heels.

"Keep your visual on our line!" Daren bellows over the gunfire. "Kelrim is the only one with the street map!"

"Understood!" I yell up to the rooftops. "Melindra! Give me the updraft!"

Melindra flicks her wrist. Rushing wind curls tight beneath my boots, hurling me thirty feet into the sky. I unlimber my crossbow, nocking a heavy quarrel as Flower and I close ranks with Kate's ice platform.

Dozens of bronze spheres swivel toward us, their red lenses burning. I cock and fire, dropping two drones through their optics, but fresh reinforcements peel off the cloud deck to replace them.

The sheer volume of fire blinds my peripheral vision. A drone drops silently out of the sun behind my left shoulder, its capacitor screaming as it unleashes a freezing beam point-blank into my spine.

Frost coats my coat in an instant, biting deep into my flesh. My hardened aura absorbs the worst of the crystallization, preventing my organs from freezing solid, though my muscles lock in agony. I grit my teeth, whip my crossbow around, and drive a steel bolt straight through the drone's optic lens. The casing shatters in a hail of frozen shards.

"Barry!" Flower darts in, four orbiting spheres of white-hot flame spiraling around my torso until warmth thaws the frost in my coat. "I've got you!"

Down in the street, Daren waves from a wooden doorway fifty paces away, ushering Kelrim, Leila, and Hadrik inside before slipping past the threshold.

With the shop secured, we pour fire and frost into the remaining swarm until the surviving spheres bank sharply and retreat into the cloud layer.

We glide down to the street cobblestones just as Daren pushes Pete's front door open, satchels secured over his chest plate.

}
#if(v_combat_technique >= 2 || v_aura_hardening < 3) {
"Daren, push for the shop," I call out. "Flower and I are backing them up. That barrier is about to crack."

"Petal and I are airborne!" Flower shouts, twin jets of orange fire flaring from her heels.

"Keep your visual on our line!" Daren bellows over the gunfire. "Kelrim is the only one with the street map!"

"Understood!" I yell up to the rooftops. "Melindra! Give me the updraft!"

Melindra flicks her wrist. Rushing wind curls tight beneath my boots, hurling me thirty feet into the sky. I unlimber my crossbow, nocking a heavy quarrel as Flower and I close ranks with Kate's ice platform.

}
#if(v_combat_technique >= 2) {
My combat technique training keeps the aerial melee readable. I anticipate the attack angles of the bronze spheres, ducking under kinetic slugs and leading crossbow shots directly into their propulsion seams. Flower showers the flank in white-hot flame while Kate's icicles spear optics.

Down the avenue, Daren waves from the threshold of Pete's shop, pulling Kelrim, Leila, and Hadrik inside.

We hold the air corridor for another thirty seconds until the surviving drones register unsustainable casualties, break formation, and retreat in a high climbing bank.

We drop to the flagstones as Daren and Hadrik emerge with full satchels.

}
#if(v_aura_hardening < 3 && v_combat_technique < 2) {
The swarm overwhelms our defensive perimeter. A bronze sphere drops from a blind angle above my left shoulder, discharging a concentrated freeze ray directly into my back.

Glacial frost encases my torso in a heartbeat. Ice crystals rip through my lungs and freeze the blood in my veins. I catch a blurred glimpse of Flower diving toward me with open palms of flame, but the cold reaches my heart first. The light snaps out.

}
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06a-Entrance, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06a-Entrance) if (v_aura_hardening >= 3 || v_combat_technique >= 2)
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_aura_hardening < 3 && v_combat_technique < 2)
