ID: B3-Ch06a-Silent
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch6_selected == 3) {
Silence stretches on the line.

"Barry, do you copy?" Daren raises his voice, pressing the speaker to his ear.

Static hisses from the casing. Nothing else.

Kelrim unhooks a smaller transceiver from beneath his white vestment. "Barry, this is Kelrim! Are you at the terminal?"

"Dead air," Daren says after another five seconds. "Something is suppressing the transmission band."

Hadrik scowls at the sky. "I bet good coin the Overseer jammed the frequency. That explains how the royal guard tracked our approach. The construct sold our position."

I turn to the bronze sphere hovering behind us. "Well, Overseer? Care to explain?"

"Input does not match survey parameters," the machine chirps. "To repeat the prompt—"

"Never mind," I mutter.

"Move toward the main thoroughfare," Daren says. "With luck, the interference drops once we clear these brick walls."

"Step quickly," Melindra says. "The royal guards are advancing at a steady march, but if Gontrok breaks into a sprint, he covers the distance in two minutes."

"If Gontrok runs ahead alone, leave the opening to me," Hadrik says as we stride toward the avenue. "I have several adjustments to demonstrate."

The bronze drone drifts silently behind my shoulder, though the automated survey chimes have ceased.

"If he charges alone, shouldn't we overwhelm him collectively?" Kate asks Hadrik.

"You won't drop Gontrok before his unit arrives," Hadrik says flatly. "If the rest of the guard crashes into our flank while we're tied up with Gontrok, they roll our line in thirty seconds. I hold his focus. You keep your guard up for ambushes. The last thing we need is someone caught cold before the melee starts."

"Fair point," Kate concedes. "Let's hope the drills hold up under steel."

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_selected != 3) {
Silence stretches on the line.

"Barry, do you copy?" Daren raises his voice, pressing the speaker to his ear.

Static hisses from the casing. Nothing else.

Kelrim unhooks a smaller transceiver from beneath his white vestment. "Barry, this is Kelrim! Are you at the terminal?"

"Dead air," Daren says after another five seconds. "Something is suppressing the transmission band."

Hadrik scowls at the sky. "I bet good coin the Overseer jammed the frequency. That explains how the royal guard tracked our approach. The construct sold our position."

"Move toward the main thoroughfare," Daren says. "With luck, the interference drops once we clear these brick walls."

"Step quickly," Melindra says. "The royal guards are advancing at a steady march, but if Gontrok breaks into a sprint, he covers the distance in two minutes."

"If Gontrok runs ahead alone, leave the opening to me," Hadrik says as we stride toward the avenue. "I have several adjustments to demonstrate."

"If he charges alone, shouldn't we overwhelm him collectively?" Kate asks Hadrik.

"You won't drop Gontrok before his unit arrives," Hadrik says flatly. "If the rest of the guard crashes into our flank while we're tied up with Gontrok, they roll our line in thirty seconds. I hold his focus. You keep your guard up for ambushes. The last thing we need is someone caught cold before the melee starts."

"Fair point," Kate concedes. "Let's hope the drills hold up under steel."

}
"If things turn desperate... I have an offensive weave," Kelrim says hesitantly as we reach the wider street. "A modified variant of a restorative spell from last month. When I miscast it, the backlash nearly stopped my heart, but it induced violent nausea in the subject. If I amplify the output, it could incapacitate—"

"Kelrim, I am not permitting a suicide cast to make a royal guard gag," Daren says firmly.

"An amplified cast delivers more than simple nausea," Kelrim argues. "The priority is delivering the satchels to the ward. If we fall on this street, the patients die—"

"No," Daren cuts him off. "We hold the line. You keep to the rear and cast combat restoration when someone takes a wound. Clear?"

"Understood," Kelrim murmurs. He glances down the avenue. "We've put space between ourselves and the shop. Try the transceiver again."

Daren and Kelrim both tap their casings, calling for the operator. Static crackles over both speakers. Barry Thundercloud remains completely unreachable.

