choice(""Maybe we could go a little further down the road and try calling him again from there?"", B3-Ch06a-Further, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06a-Further, v_b3_ch6_preparing = 0)


ID: B3-Ch06a-Further
TEXT:

"Maybe we could go a little further down the road and try calling him again from there?"

"Worth a try," Daren says, scanning the rooftops. "Though I doubt we avoid a clash at this stage."

Kelrim turns his transceiver dial as we advance down the avenue. "Roberta, can you hear me?" he calls into the bronze grill. "Roberta, respond!"

"Who are you calling?" Daren asks.

"A head nurse in the quarantine sector," Kelrim says. "If local interference blocks the transit vault directly, perhaps she can run down the hall and alert Barry in person."

"The seredium density is too thick," Kate says. "Outside of the dedicated teleporter receiver, signals cannot pierce the underground base. Daren's enchanted units barely manage the transit room, and those rely on matched frequencies."

"My transceivers are tuned as matched pairs," Daren confirms. "On open public frequencies, they perform no better than market stock."

"Understood," Kelrim sighs. "Let's try Barry directly once more."

Daren halts beneath an overhanging awning. "This clearance should give us a cleaner angle."

He taps the rune plate and raises the device. "Barry! Do you copy?"

"Barry, respond!" Kelrim shouts into his unit.

"Thundercloud!" Daren bellows.

A cool, measured voice cuts through the static: "Barry, why are you ignoring the console?"

"Albert?" the operator's voice crackles over the line. "I didn't hear you enter the vault!"

"Naturally," Albert's dry tone returns. "I'm an assassin. I came to check the refugee muster, only to find you staring blankly at a howling transceiver. What is happening on the surface?"

"A distortion field is choking their localized sector," the operator says quickly. "The teleporter cannot lock their aura frequencies, and outward transmissions fail to cross the barrier."

"Barry, we read you now!" Daren shouts into the casing. "We shifted positions. Try locking the array again!"

choice("Continue", B3-Ch06a-Further2, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06a-Further2)


ID: B3-Ch06a-Further2
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch5_fight < 4) {
"You can hear me?" Thundercloud says. "Hold your ground! Engaging the transfer sequence now!"

Chimes and ticking relays echo from the console for ten agonizing seconds. The air around our boots remains dead calm.

"It isn't taking," Thundercloud's voice tightens. "The array won't recognize your field signatures. Regulate your breathing—if your auras fluctuate wildly, the lock slips!"

"Hard to keep our auras serene with five killers closing in, Thundercloud," Hadrik grunts.

"You claimed you could handle the royal guard on your own terms," Albert's voice drifts over the line. "Here is your opportunity to prove it."

"Don't sulk when we topple this regime and put you out of work," Hadrik retorts.

"I will manage," Albert says coolly.

Daren closes the casing. "Melindra, time to contact?"

"Three minutes if they hold their current pace," Melindra says. "They were well out when I first tracked them."

"Taking their time," Hadrik notes.

"They know our extraction is jammed," Melindra says. "They didn't even bother dispatching trainees as harriers. They set the distortion field deliberately."

Hadrik rolls his shoulders, knuckles cracking. "A wide, straight avenue with nowhere to run. Perfect for an honest brawl."

}
#if(v_b3_ch5_fight >= 4) {
"You can hear me?" Thundercloud says. "Hold your ground! Engaging the transfer sequence now!"

Chimes and ticking relays echo from the console for ten agonizing seconds. The air around our boots remains dead calm.

"It isn't taking," Thundercloud's voice tightens. "The array won't recognize your field signatures. Regulate your breathing—if your auras fluctuate wildly, the lock slips!"

"Hard to keep our auras serene with five killers closing in, Thundercloud," Hadrik grunts.

"If extraction fails, can you transit me to their coordinates instead?" Albert asks over the line.

"Yes," Thundercloud says. "I can drop you into an adjacent alley."

"Align the grid," Albert says.

Daren blinks at the speaker. "You're deploying to assist us, Albert?"

"I hold zero fondness for your party," Albert replies. "Your intrusion triggered this lockdown and displaced hundreds of civilians. But treaty makes us allies, and I do not neglect an oath. Stay alive until I reach the street."

"Leave a guard or two for your daggers," Hadrik grins. "No promises on the captain, though."

"Understood," Albert says dryly.

"Grid locked, Albert," Thundercloud calls. "Ready?"

"Transmit."

A shrill resonant whine echoes over the line, followed by the muffled rush of displaced air as Albert shifts out of the underground vault.

Daren closes the casing. "Melindra, time to contact?"

"Three minutes if they hold their current pace," Melindra says. "They were well out when I first tracked them."

"Taking their time," Hadrik notes.

"They know our extraction is jammed," Melindra says. "They didn't even bother dispatching trainees as harriers. They set the distortion field deliberately."

Hadrik rolls his shoulders, knuckles cracking. "A wide, straight avenue with nowhere to run. Perfect for an honest brawl."

}
