ID: B3-Ch06a-Focus
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch6_secret == 0) {
"This is clearly not working. Can't we focus on preparing for the fight instead?"

"We covered deployment in the briefing," Daren says, resting his hand on his pommel. "Hadrik takes Gontrok, I engage the captain, and the rest of you neutralize the auxiliary casters before they establish control. Melindra, count the line."

"Seven signatures closing on our quadrant," Melindra says. "Gontrok, the captain, and Loyrang. Three auxiliary mages accompany them, along with one un-attuned combatant who relies on lessathi relics."

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_tie == 0 && v_b3_ch6_secret != 0) {
"This is clearly not working. Can't we focus on preparing for the fight instead?"

"We covered deployment in the briefing," Daren says, resting his hand on his pommel. "Hadrik takes Gontrok, I engage the captain, and the rest of you neutralize the auxiliary casters before they establish control. Melindra, count the line."

"Seven signatures closing on our quadrant," Melindra says. "Gontrok, the captain, and Loyrang. Three auxiliary mages accompany them, along with one un-attuned combatant who relies on lessathi relics."

"Loyrang?" I frown. "He swore he was heading for the gates."

"A patrol likely intercepted his route and turned him around," Melindra says. "He had little choice."

"Terrific," I mutter.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_tie == 1 && v_b3_ch6_secret != 0) {
"This is clearly not working. Can't we focus on preparing for the fight instead?"

"We covered deployment in the briefing," Daren says, resting his hand on his pommel. "Hadrik takes Gontrok, I engage the captain, and the rest of you neutralize the auxiliary casters before they establish control. Melindra, count the line."

"Six signatures closing on our quadrant," Melindra says. "Gontrok and the captain lead. Three auxiliary mages accompany them, along with one un-attuned combatant who relies on lessathi relics."

}
"What of the black-robed assassin from our first surface run?" Daren asks. "Do you track him?"

"No," Melindra says. "His rings mask his signature completely. He could be fifty paces away."

Daren looks toward Flower's necklace. "Arraka, do you sense a suppressed field?"

"Obviously," Arraka's voice drifts up.

"Will you alert us when he enters striking distance?" Daren asks.

"If I feel like it," she snorts.

"Reassuring," Daren sighs. "Melindra, time to contact?"

"Three minutes if they hold their current pace," Melindra says. "They were well out when I first tracked them."

"Taking their time," Hadrik notes.

"They know our extraction is jammed," Melindra says. "They didn't even bother dispatching trainees as harriers. They set the distortion field deliberately."

Hadrik rolls his shoulders, knuckles cracking. "A wide, straight avenue with nowhere to run. Perfect for an honest brawl."

